  Key Analytical Findings:
  1. psi_prime(N) is an almost-periodic sum of high-frequency sines over prime powers.
     It does NOT decay as N -> inf; it oscillates indefinitely with O(1) envelope.
  2. psi_pole(N) decays as O(1/N) as expected from the zeta pole integral.
  3. psi_arch(N) provides a smooth, slowly varying Mellin baseline.
  4. Because psi_total(N) oscillates with O(1) amplitude, a_N / sqrt(2) = sqrt(2)*N*psi_total(N)
     oscillates wildly in sign and its envelope grows linearly as O(N).

